; xact_t::hash feeds the auxiliary date (and each posting's checkin and
; checkout) as boost's optional operator<< spelled them: "--" when empty,
; else a space and the value.  Hash: tags already written into journals
; depend on that spelling, so it must not change with the optional type.

2024/01/01=2024/01/05 (C1) Aux dated
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 No aux date
    Expenses:Food    $20.00
    Assets:Cash

test print --hashes=sha512 --columns=80
2024/01/01=2024/01/05 (C1) Aux dated
    ; Hash: 28ba7c6b113e489212f98f259bc54e5498da43a4056e29f18f4a88633d280f1120eb94caaff2e2ab396154be04193a5018f8692d502f501c7feb4b7f5bcc8e98
    Expenses:Food                             $10.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 No aux date
    ; Hash: 72a54de34577971ae2e14d82e1f59196d9242d5ec8c5b5d8565ec106f41674acce1b217de84ce763fb7a381554e2ddde1b07f1fb65b99da84d21a73d121240a1
    Expenses:Food                             $20.00
    Assets:Cash
end test

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/hash-optional-fields.dat bal --hashes=sha512
             $-30.00  Assets:Cash
              $30.00  Expenses:Food
--------------------
                   0
end test
